\begin{tabular}{lll}
\toprule
Razorpay Payment Method & Transaction Type & Description \\
\midrule
Credit Card & PAYMENT & Card-based payment with credit facility \\
Debit Card & PAYMENT & Card-based payment tied to bank account \\
UPI & TRANSFER & Direct bank account transfer via UPI \\
Net Banking & TRANSFER & Direct bank transfer via internet banking \\
Wallet & CASH_IN & Pre-loaded wallet balance transaction \\
EMI & DEBIT & Extended payment with installments \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Mapping of Razorpay Payment Methods to Transaction Types}
\label{table:razorpay_mapping}
\end{table}

\subsection{Training Methodology}

The neural network is trained using the following methodology:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Loss Function:} Binary Cross-Entropy Loss with Logits (BCEWithLogitsLoss), which combines a sigmoid layer and binary cross-entropy loss for numerical stability
    \item \textbf{Optimizer:} Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 0.001 and weight decay of 1e-5 for regularization
    \item \textbf{Batch Size:} 64 transactions per batch, balancing computational efficiency and gradient accuracy
    \item \textbf{Training Epochs:} 100 epochs with early stopping based on validation loss plateau
    \item \textbf{Data Split:} 70\% training, 15\% validation, 15\% testing
    \item \textbf{Class Balancing:} Weighted sampling to address the class imbalance between fraudulent and legitimate transactions \cite{fraud_nn}
    \item \textbf{Data Augmentation:} Synthetic minority oversampling for rare fraud patterns
\end{itemize}

The model is trained on a combination of PaySim synthetic data and real-world Razorpay transaction data, with sensitive information anonymized. In simulation mode, the system can generate synthetic training data when no pre-trained model or historical data is available.

